# Inside the pyramid (7:23): the lizard men who hiss "are wary, but not hostile" (PARLAY: the enemy
# of my enemy), and the shackled slaves in the pumping room, who when freed (PARLAY, NICE) give
# the friend word for their tribe in the swamp (journal entry 35; the Clue Book's way into the
# lizard men's keep).
parley 7:23 THEY ARE WARY, BUT NOT HOSTILE
parley 7:23 THEY RECOIL IN FEAR
# The rocks room (7:22 14,7, event 14): the first visit flashes the party into 7:23; after that
# it asks GO BACK / MOVE ON / THROW A ROCK. MOVE ON goes to 7:23 unless a thrown rock has turned
# the teleporter (0x4A4D bit 0), and then MOVE ON again does. (The sweep recorded this exit on
# the first visit, so the lab's exits.txt keeps no picks for it.)
answer 7:22 [4A4D&1=0] THROW A ROCK|MOVE ON
# Chat 23: with bit 0 set (7:23's room or the dial sent the party back), MOVE ON goes elsewhere in
# 7:22 (0xA030 -> 0x992D: 5,11): throw a rock first, which flips the bit (0xA12B).
answer 7:22 [4A4D&1=1] THROW A ROCK|THROW A ROCK
# 7:23's rocks room: 7:22's sends the party in with 0x4A4D bit 0 set, and MOVE ON with it set
# goes back to 7:22 (a loop). THROW A ROCK flips it; then MOVE ON goes to 11,3, the way to
# the dial, the mage and the desk.
answer 7:23 THROW A ROCK|THROW A ROCK,MOVE ON
# The dial (5,0) sets where the teleporters at 6,0 and 3,13 go (0x4A50: BLUE 7:22, COPPER 4,9,
# SILVER 7,0, GOLD 14,13); left as it is. The shackled lizard men in the pumping room (5,4) are
# the ones to free: 0x4A52 bit 0 brings the old lizard man out in the keep (8:16).
answer 7:23 DO YOU WISH TO CHANGE THE SETTING|NO
